description:
FILED + FIXED s518e (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-17) from the Type-Tiny census cause run (chunk 1, scratch/s518e/causes1.tsv): 20 of the 92 FAIL files died "Undefined subroutine &Test::Builder::Module::builder called" -- 18 of them are files real perl SKIPS (`use Test::Requires 'Moose'` etc.: the optional module is absent), 2 (03-leak.t, Test::LeakTrace is XS) run in perl.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs main ff4c1500):

    package Req; our @ISA = ('Test::Builder::Module');
    package main; use Test::More;
    my $b = Req->builder;
    $b->skip_all("needs Frob") if !defined $b->has_plan;

perl: `1..0 # SKIP needs Frob`.  PCL: dies, no TAP.

FIX (cl/pcl-test.lisp, the harness's Test::Builder section): Test::Builder::Module->builder = the singleton; ->has_plan (undef / "no_plan" / the count), ->skip(REASON) (one skip row, no `last SKIP`), ->skip_all(REASON) (= plan skip_all), ->is_passing.  skip / skip_all are SHADOWED in Test::Builder first: the package uses :pcl and pl-skip / pl-skip_all are the TAP layer's own functions -- a plain defun redefined them (caught on the first probe).

GUARD: Pl/t/universal-01.t rows 12-13, inverse-verified on a main extraction.
